{%- comment -%}
  The assertions, read straight from _data/ontology.yml. The graph shows the shape
  of this; the list is where the claims are actually legible, with their kind,
  their confidence and their source.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign onto = site.data.ontology -%}
{%- if onto and onto.assertions -%}
  <div class="on-wrap">
    <h2 class="on-h">Ontology</h2>
    <p class="on-lead">
      The <a href="{{ '/research/#graph' | relative_url }}">knowledge graph</a> records which of these notes
      discusses which concept. This is a different thing: what kind of entity each concept is, and what
      I hold to be true between them. Every line below is an assertion, so every line is disputable, and
      the ones resting on published work carry the source. <strong>{{ onto.assertions | size }}</strong>
      assertions over <strong>{{ onto.concepts | size }}</strong> concepts, in
      <strong>{{ onto.relations | size }}</strong> relations.
    </p>

    <div class="on-types">
      {%- for t in onto.colors %}
        {%- assign tname = t[0] %}
        {%- assign n = 0 %}
        {%- for c in onto.concepts %}{% if c[1] == tname %}{% assign n = n | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        <span class="on-type" title="{{ onto.types[tname] }}">
          <i style="background: {{ t[1].light }}"></i>{{ tname }}<b>{{ n }}</b>
        </span>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    {%- for r in onto.relations %}
      {%- assign rname = r[0] %}
      <section class="on-rel">
        <h3 class="on-rel-h">{{ rname }}</h3>
        <p class="on-rel-sig">
          <span class="on-dr">{{ r[1].domain | join: " · " }}</span>
          <span class="on-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <span class="on-dr">{{ r[1].range | join: " · " }}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="on-rel-gloss">{{ r[1].gloss }}</p>
        <ul class="on-list">
          {%- for a in onto.assertions %}
            {%- if a[2] == rname %}
              <li class="on-item">
                <span class="on-triple">
                  <span class="on-c" style="--t: {{ onto.colors[onto.concepts[a[1]]].light }}">{{ a[1] }}</span>
                  <span class="on-rel-in">{{ rname }}</span>
                  <span class="on-c" style="--t: {{ onto.colors[onto.concepts[a[3]]].light }}">{{ a[3] }}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="on-meta">
                  <span class="on-kind on-k-{{ a[4] }}">{%- case a[4] -%}
                    {%- when 'D' -%}definitional{%- when 'M' -%}methodological{%- else -%}empirical{%- endcase -%}</span>
                  <span class="on-conf">{{ a[5] }} confidence</span>
                  <span class="on-id">{{ a[0] }}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="on-note">{{ a[6] }}</span>
                {%- if a[7] %}
                  {%- assign src = a[7] %}
                  {%- if src contains 'arXiv:' %}
                    {%- assign aid = src | remove: 'arXiv:' %}
                    <a class="on-src" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/{{ aid }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">arXiv:{{ aid }}</a>
                  {%- else %}
                    <a class="on-src" href="https://doi.org/{{ src }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi:{{ src }}</a>
                  {%- endif %}
                {%- else %}
                  <span class="on-src on-nosrc">no source asserted</span>
                {%- endif %}
              </li>
            {%- endif %}
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </section>
    {%- endfor %}

    <p class="on-foot">
      Absence of an edge means not asserted, not false. <code>doesNotEstablish</code> is itself a positive
      claim of non-entailment, not a claim of incompatibility. None of this determines whether a particular
      trained model uses a shortcut; that needs an experiment.
    </p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .on-wrap { margin-top: 3.2rem; padding-top: 1.6rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--global-divider-color); }
    .on-h { margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
    .on-lead { font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 46rem; opacity: .88; }
    .on-types { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem; margin: 1rem 0 1.8rem; }
    .on-type {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; cursor: help;
      padding: .26rem .6rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: .74rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--global-divider-color);
    }
    .on-type i { width: .55rem; height: .55rem; border-radius: 50%; flex: 0 0 auto; }
    .on-type b { font-weight: 700; opacity: .45; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

    .on-rel { margin: 0 0 1.7rem; }
    .on-rel-h { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
    .on-rel-sig { margin: .15rem 0 .1rem; font-size: .72rem; opacity: .5; }
    .on-arrow { margin: 0 .35rem; }
    .on-rel-gloss { margin: 0 0 .6rem; font-size: .84rem; opacity: .72; max-width: 46rem; line-height: 1.6; }

    .on-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    /* A rule per assertion rather than a card each: fifty-eight boxes would read
       as a wall, and the claim is the thing worth seeing. */
    .on-item { padding: .6rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--global-divider-color); }
    .on-triple { display: block; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.5; }
    .on-c { font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--t); }
    .on-rel-in {
      margin: 0 .35rem; font-size: .76rem; opacity: .5;
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    }
    .on-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem; margin: .25rem 0 .2rem; font-size: .68rem; }
    .on-kind { font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .on-k-D { color: var(--global-text-color-light); }
    .on-k-M { color: var(--global-theme-color); }
    .on-k-E { color: var(--global-theme-color); opacity: .75; }
    .on-conf, .on-id { opacity: .45; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .on-note { display: block; font-size: .84rem; line-height: 1.6; opacity: .78; max-width: 48rem; }
    .on-src { display: inline-block; margin-top: .25rem; font-size: .7rem; opacity: .6;
              font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .on-nosrc { font-style: italic; opacity: .38; }
    .on-foot { margin-top: 1.6rem; font-size: .82rem; opacity: .6; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 46rem; }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
